From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: retry RX repair across split Oblivion image regions

The 0975 run found the previously observed executable image page at
0x004a7e60, but sceKernelVirtualQuery reported a split region beginning at
0x004a4000 after an adjacent page's protection changed. Accept queried
subregions contained within the measured main-image span instead of requiring
the old unsplit mapping boundary. Keep the retry limited to instruction-fetch
faults in that image span and verify RX before retrying.

---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -2860,9 +2860,9 @@
                 range_start = (uintptr_t)info.start;
                 range_end = (uintptr_t)info.end;
             }
-            if (!query_rc && ((range_start == 0x0049c000 && range_end == 0x004a8000) ||
-                              (range_start == 0x004a8000 && range_end == 0x004ac000)) &&
-                page >= range_start && page + 0x4000 <= range_end &&
+            if (!query_rc && range_start >= 0x00400000 &&
+                range_end <= 0x00a28000 && page >= range_start &&
+                page + 0x4000 <= range_end &&
                 (info.protection & PROT_READ) && !(info.protection & PROT_EXEC))
             {
                 mprotect_rc = __wine_ps5_mprotect( (void *)page, 0x4000,
-- 
2.43.0
